From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: domicile CI <ci@domicile.invalid>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] domicile: a canvas read-back does not wait for the screen's
 flip

A 2D canvas read-back (getImageData) took about one frame on a tty:
9.4ms at 120Hz, where Chromium nested in the same desktop takes 0.45ms.
A page reading back a hundred small canvases froze for over a second.

GbmSurfaceless completed each swap at submission with the commit's
out-fence as its release fence. The fence signals at the flip. Viz makes
the GPU wait on it before drawing into the released buffer, and the
display shares its GL context with raster, so every GPU job queued after
that draw waited for the flip too. A read-back blocks in glReadPixels
until its own draw is done (stack from lyra: _mesa_ReadPixels ->
amdgpu_bo_wait).

- OnSubmission no longer completes the swap. It completes in
  OnPresentation, at the flip, with no release fence, as it does on a
  device that gives no out-fence. The buffer viz gets back is off the
  screen by then, so its next draw needs no wait.

Verified: not built. This repository cannot build Chromium; the engine
job builds it on `crux`.
---
 ui/ozone/platform/drm/gpu/gbm_surfaceless.cc | 9 +++++----
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/ui/ozone/platform/drm/gpu/gbm_surfaceless.cc b/ui/ozone/platform/drm/gpu/gbm_surfaceless.cc
index 151bfe6..9925b6a 100644
--- a/ui/ozone/platform/drm/gpu/gbm_surfaceless.cc
+++ b/ui/ozone/platform/drm/gpu/gbm_surfaceless.cc
@@ -236,10 +236,11 @@ void GbmSurfaceless::FenceRetired(uint32_t frame_id) {
 void GbmSurfaceless::OnSubmission(gfx::SwapResult result,
                                   gfx::GpuFenceHandle release_fence) {
   submitted_frame_->swap_result = result;
-  if (!release_fence.is_null()) {
-    std::move(submitted_frame_->completion_callback)
-        .Run(gfx::SwapCompletionResult(result, std::move(release_fence)));
-  }
+  // Domicile's engine fork: the swap completes at presentation, with no
+  // release fence. The fence is the commit's out-fence, which signals at the
+  // flip. Viz makes the GPU wait on it before drawing into a released buffer,
+  // and the display shares its GL context with raster, so every later GPU
+  // job, a canvas read-back among them, would wait for the flip.
 }
 
 void GbmSurfaceless::OnPresentation(const gfx::PresentationFeedback& feedback) {
